<title>PHILIPPINES: Kazakhstan gets $50 mln loan to rehabilitate roads.</title>
<headline>Kazakhstan gets $50 mln loan to rehabilitate roads.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Asian Development Bank (ADB) said on Tuesday it had approved a $50 million loan to Kazakhstan for the rehabilitation of its national road network.</p>
<p>The loan carries an interest rate of 6.82 percent and will be repaid in 24 years including a four-year grace period, the Manila-based multilateral financing institution said.</p>
<p>The project is expected to be completed by year 2000.</p>
</text>
